      <attrChanges atrAnchor="atr">
        <attrChange attrType="Documentation (VI Properties)" detailDesc="changed from &quot;Caraya unit test for Get Menu Action.vi, generated by lvai_generate_test.&#xA;&#xA;One static subVI call per case. Every assertion takes its error in from Define Test rather than from the assertion before it, so a failing case cannot stop a later one - chaining them silently loses cases, measured.&#xA;&#xA;The error cluster carries the FIRST failure only. Read the JUnit report for all of them.&quot; to &quot;Caraya unit test for Get Menu Action.vi.&#xA;&#xA;One static subVI call per case. All cases share ONE fixture menu - the application's main menu as Get Main Menu.vi returns it since feature #47 (Fast Cash $100 top left, Fast Cash $50 bottom right). The Menu constant is an instance of the typedef ATM Menu.ctl and every expected constant an instance of ATM States.ctl, so they follow the typedefs when the states enum grows. Do not replace them with unlinked copies: Caraya compares the enum's item list too, and a stale copy fails every case although the numbers are equal.&#xA;&#xA;Case 1: top right button (Right, index 0) selects Deposit Prompt.&#xA;Case 2: middle left button (Left, index 1) selects Balance Inquiry.&#xA;Case 3: no button (index -1) returns None.&#xA;Case 4: top left button (Left, index 0) selects Fast Cash $100.&#xA;Case 5: bottom right button (Right, index 2) still selects Fast Cash, the $50 state.&#xA;&#xA;Every assertion takes its error in from Define Test rather than from the assertion before it, so a failing case cannot stop a later one. The error cluster carries the FIRST failure only. Read the JUnit report for all of them.&quot;" diffType="description text"/>
      </attrChanges>
